      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Conformal methods gave exact, broadly applicable results for two-dimensional critical phenomena and reshaped statistical physics and field theory.",
        "attribution": "Zamolodchikov and Cardy developed key results connecting conformal symmetry to exact critical behavior; Polyakov's foundational work on conformal invariance helped establish the framework.",
        "maturity": "The theory has been tested and applied across decades of critical systems, with its mathematical structure well understood.",
        "uncertainties": [
