        "Alan H. Guth",
        "Andrei Linde",
        "Viatcheslav Mukhanov"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Inflation offers a compelling account of early-universe expansion and primordial structure, with consequences tested through precise cosmological observations.",
        "attribution": "Guth and Linde developed influential inflationary proposals; Mukhanov made seminal contributions to the theory of primordial perturbations.",
        "maturity": "The framework's observable predictions have been developed in detail, but the inflationary mechanism itself has not been uniquely identified.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "There is no direct confirmation of inflation or a settled model, and primordial gravitational waves remain undetected."
        ]
      }
    },
