        "Immanuel Bloch",
        "Rainer Blatt",
        "Juan Ignacio Cirac"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Controlled atoms have made quantum simulation of many-body physics experimentally accessible and enabled precise tests of quantum dynamics.",
        "attribution": "Cirac supplied influential theoretical foundations, while Bloch and Blatt led distinct experimental routes using ultracold atoms and trapped ions.",
        "maturity": "The platforms are highly controlled and productive, though the strongest demonstrations of broadly useful quantum simulation are still developing.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The candidate combines different platforms and goals, making the precise discovery and appropriate attribution uncertain."
        ]
      }
    },
