      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "WMAP's precision mapping of cosmic microwave background anisotropies transformed cosmology into a precision science and constrained the universe's fundamental parameters.",
        "attribution": "Bennett led the mission, Page made major instrumental and observational contributions, and Spergel played a central role in extracting cosmological implications.",
        "maturity": "The maps and their scientific conclusions have been extensively checked and strengthened by later measurements.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The work extends the COBE discovery and was followed by Planck, so the distinct Nobel-scale contribution and mission-wide credit require careful definition."
        ]
